Mutant: capture_hold releases the hold's reservation after spending, not before.

The capture boundary bug: the debit entries land while the hold still counts as
held, so for that moment the account's available amount is short by the whole
hold. Any capture where amount + hold > what was available before the hold
(capturing the last of the funds, or most of them) is refused by the database's
overdraft CHECK. The README's original planted bug (a partial capture releasing
only the captured amount) can't be replayed: since migration 005 the release is
done by a trigger from the hold's own amount, so this is the equivalent mutant on
the same boundary in today's code.

Check that the tests catch it (each target must fail with it, pass without it):
  python scripts/mutation_check.py tests/mutants/capture_releases_after_spending.patch \
      tests/test_holds.py::test_a_capture_at_the_funds_boundary_succeeds tests/test_invariants.py

